# expo-glass-effect (GlassView) constraints

When using `GlassView` or `GlassContainer` from `expo-glass-effect`:

## 1. isInteractive: set once, remount to toggle

The `isInteractive` prop can only be set once on mount and **cannot be changed dynamically** after the component has been rendered. To toggle interactive behavior, remount the component with a different `key`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD – toggling isInteractive dynamically causes incorrect behavior
<GlassView isInteractive={isInteractive} />

// ✅ GOOD – remount with a key when isInteractive changes
<GlassView key={isInteractive ? 'interactive' : 'static'} isInteractive={isInteractive} />
```

## 2. No opacity &lt; 1 on GlassView or its parents

Do **not** use `opacity` values less than `1` on `GlassView` or any parent view. It causes the effect to render incorrectly (see Apple's UIVisualEffectView docs and [expo/expo#41024](https://github.com/expo/expo/issues/41024)).

For fade in/out, use the **`animate`** and **`animationDuration`** props in **`glassEffectStyle`** instead of opacity.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD – opacity on GlassView or parent breaks the effect
<View style={{ opacity: 0.8 }}>
  <GlassView style={styles.glass} />
</View>

// ✅ GOOD – use glassEffectStyle for fading
<GlassView
  style={styles.glass}
  glassEffectStyle={{ animate: true, animationDuration: 200 }}
/>
```

Keep `GlassView` and its ancestor views at `opacity: 1` (or omit opacity).
